    "evidence": "On 2026-07-30 the deployment inventory was re-derived. The Ethereum ReceiptToken 0x48f9e38f3070ad8945dfeae3fa70987722e3d89c read paused() = false at block 25648350 and its verified source exposes no holder blacklist or transfer hook; the BNB OFT 0x60B14ec49874Af1BA471685cb11132101aeBdF09 exposes no pause or blacklist selector. The decisive surface is the Tempo TIP-20 IUSD 0x20c000000000000000000000AB02D39df30bd17E: the TIP20Factory TokenCreated event at Tempo block 12424756 names creation admin 0xa11ce67cd9ad7295948a681617aa81e0523e0679; RoleMembershipUpdated logs show DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE granted to the infiniFi admin Safe 0x80608f852d152024c0a2087b16939235fec2400c at block 22529597 and the creation admin's own DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE revoked at block 22529608, with no subsequent role events through Tempo block 32484367, while ISSUER_ROLE is held by the reviewed LayerZero OFT adapter 0xfA339b5a3AD03fd9Ff048F574636b60d0FC7538A. getThreshold() = 4 confirms the 4-of-7 Safe is live on Tempo. Under the TIP-20 specification, DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE can immediately set the built-in always-reject policy or any TIP-403 blocklist policy via changeTransferPolicyId and can grant PAUSE_ROLE; the current paused() = false and transferPolicyId() = 1 (always-allow) are settings, not bounds on reach. The infiniFi Safe can therefore policy-block or pause IUSD transfers on Tempo today, so the asset-level direct holder-intervention posture is reviewed true (individual reach), superseding the 2026-07-22 possible.",
    "reviewer": "Kimi T38 unknown-reduction wave 2",
